From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Draven <dravengarden@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 01:05:01 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Await the natively configured Cowboy MCP servers at session
 start

The Provider launcher names the MCP servers its native bridge injects
through `-c mcp_servers.*` in COWBOY_CODEX_AWAIT_MCP_SERVERS. With a
positive `mcpStartupAwaitTimeoutMs`, a session open awaits and reports
them beside the request's `mcpServers`. Managed profiles never wait.

Cowboy-Delta: configured-mcp-startup-wait
Upstream: not-proposed
Drop-When: upstream awaits natively configured MCP servers, or Cowboy passes its servers as ACP mcpServers
Tests: src/__tests__/CodexACPAgent/cowboy-configured-mcp-wait.test.ts

